{
  "dom_id": "step-q175509",
  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "Find the truth set of $\u00acP(x)$ given the following predicate defined over the universal set of integers between $-3$ and $3,$ inclusive: \n\n$\\,$ $P(x):$ ${x}^{2}=4$",
  "worked_solution": "The truth set of $\u00acP(x)$ is the *complement* of the truth set of $P(x):$\n\n$$\n{T}_{\u00acP}={\\overset{\u2015}{T}}_{P},\n$$\n\nThe truth set of $P(x)$ is the set of integers between $-3$ and $3,$ inclusive, whose square is $4,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}={-2,2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{\u00acP} & ={\\overset{\u2015}{T}}_{P} \\\\  & =\\overset{\u2015}{{-2,2}} \\\\  & ={-3,-1,0,1,3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
